// R5900 (Emotion Engine) instruction table.
//
// X(Op, mnemonic, match, operands, flags, memsize)
//
//   match     the encoding with every operand field zero. The decoder in
//             decoder.cpp is a hand-written switch tree that mirrors the
//             hardware decode tables; tests check decode(match) == Op for
//             every row so the two cannot drift apart.
//   operands  operand syntax, shared by the disassembler and the assembler:
//               d s t      GPR in the rd / rs / rt field
//               <          5-bit shift amount (sa field)
//               i          signed 16-bit immediate
//               u          unsigned 16-bit immediate
//               p          PC-relative branch target
//               a          26-bit jump target
//               o(b)       signed offset + base GPR (rs field)
//               D S T      FPU register in the fd(sa) / fs(rd) / ft(rt) field
//               g          FPU control register (rd field)
//               G          COP0 register (rd field)
//               B          20-bit syscall / break code
//               c          10-bit trap code
//               k          cache operation (rt field)
//               h          prefetch hint (rt field)
//               V X Y      VU0 vf register in the fd / fs / ft field
//               Yb         ft with broadcast component (bits 1-0)
//               Xf Yf      fs / ft with a single-component selector (fsf / ftf)
//               Yw         ft, w component (VCLIPw)
//               e f n      VU0 vi register in the fd(id) / fs(is) / ft(it) field
//               E          VU0 control register (rd field, 0-31)
//               5          signed 5-bit immediate (sa field, VIADDI)
//               M          15-bit microprogram address (VCALLMS)
//               A Q I R    the VU0 ACC / Q / I / R registers (no encoding bits)
//               (f++) (--f) (n++) (--n) (f) (n)   vi post-increment / pre-decrement / plain
//               P          SYNC stype / PMFHL-PMTHL format (sa field; implied by mnemonic)
//               r          perf-counter register selector (bits 5-1, MFPC/MTPC)
//   flags     classification bits from r5900.h (F_*).
//   memsize   bytes touched by a load / store, else 0.
//
// A trailing '.' operand group (VU dest mask) is implied for every F_VUDEST op.

// ---- primary opcode table ---------------------------------------------------
